---
page_key: contact
title: Contact | Tomáš Zvoníček
description: Send Tomáš Zvoníček a message through the form or by email.
scripts:
    - contact.js
---

<header class="lead lead-art">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Write to me, I'll reply by email</p>
    {% include "partials/art.njk" %}
</header>

<div class="bands bands-contact">
    <section class="band">
        <h2>Message</h2>
        <form class="fields contact-form" method="post" action="/api/contact">
            <input type="hidden" name="lang" value="en" />
            <div class="fields fields-2">
                <label class="field"
                    ><span>Name</span>
                    <input type="text" name="name" required maxlength="100" autocomplete="name" />
                </label>
                <label class="field"
                    ><span>Your email</span>
                    <input type="email" name="email" required maxlength="254" autocomplete="email" />
                </label>
            </div>
            <label class="field"
                ><span>Message</span>
                <textarea name="message" rows="6" required minlength="2" maxlength="5000"></textarea>
            </label>
            <label class="contact-trap" aria-hidden="true"
                >Leave this empty <input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"
            /></label>
            <button type="submit" class="button">Send</button>
            <p class="contact-status" role="status" data-contact-status></p>
        </form>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>Or write directly to <a href="mailto:contact@zvondis.dev">contact@zvondis.dev</a>.</p>
        <p class="contact-note">
            The form sends your name, email and message to my inbox and nothing else. It isn't
            stored on this site. Details are in the <a href="/en/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
